{{!-- Every page carries the feed in its <head>, which is how a reader (and a
      browser extension) finds it without being told. `feed.xml` is a file this
      build *writes*, not a page it registers, so it has no identity and
      {{link}} cannot name it — {{absUrl}} is the helper for a path of your own.
      Absolute, because RSS autodiscovery is consumed off-site; `npx kiss-ssg
      check` still resolves it, because a URL on this site's own origin counts
      as internal. --}}
<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Aster &amp; Oak &mdash; the journal" href="{{absUrl 'feed.xml'}}">
